      "title": "Price vs. Value and the Margin of Safety",
      "description": "Ackman argues that Benjamin Graham's distinction between price (what you pay) and value (what you get) is foundational. Because predicting the future cash flows of a business is inherently difficult, investors must buy at a significant discount—a margin of safety—so that errors in valuation do not result in permanent loss of capital."
    },
    {
      "title": "Identifying Economic Moats and Predictable Businesses",
      "description": "Ackman argues that the best investments are 'non-disruptible' businesses with deep moats and predictable long-term cash flows, such as established consumer brands and content owners. Because great businesses often carry high valuations, Ackman seeks out opportunities where strong companies temporarily stumble, allowing him to acquire them at distressed prices and help fix them."
    },
