      "title": "The Alphabet AI Market Overreaction",
      "description": "Ackman argues that the market drastically overreacted when Microsoft introduced ChatGPT and Google experienced a flawed Bard demonstration, sending Google's stock down to an attractive 15 times earnings. He reasons that Alphabet possesses superior training data, massive financial resources, and top engineering talent, making its AI capabilities equal or superior to competitors while offering a high earnings yield and zero debt."
    }
  ],
